-- title:
--   From HTo G Sum₂ Avg Over₂
-- statement:
--   **Finite sums commute with two nested finite averages.**
--
--   Let $\mathcal D_\alpha$ and $\mathcal D_\beta$ be distributions on $\alpha$ and $\beta$, let $\Gamma$ and $\Delta$ be finite index sets, and let
--
--   $$
--   F:\Gamma\times\Delta\times\alpha\times\beta\to\mathrm{Error}.
--   $$
--
--   Then, without any probability or normalization assumption on the two distributions,
--
--   $$
--   \sum_{c\in\Gamma}\sum_{d\in\Delta}
--   \mathbb E_{a\sim\mathcal D_\alpha}\mathbb E_{b\sim\mathcal D_\beta}F(c,d,a,b)
--   =
--   \mathbb E_{a\sim\mathcal D_\alpha}\mathbb E_{b\sim\mathcal D_\beta}
--   \sum_{c\in\Gamma}\sum_{d\in\Delta}F(c,d,a,b).
--   $$
--
--   This finite sum-and-average interchange is used to globalize pointwise adjacent-stage formulas and to rearrange the self-consistency context average.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.fromHToG_sum₂_avgOver₂`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
